        "date": "2026-11-11T00:14:25Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ops): one machining-frame seam - OpFrame composes part_alignment and TiltedFrame\n\nPhase 1 of #763: OpFrame (crates/app/src/operation/frame.rs) is the one\nmachining-frame seam - the setup's part_alignment (#326) and the op's\n3+2 Tilt (M5.1 B) composed behind one door. collect_job reads material\nand heights through it and builds its tilt frame from\nOpFrame::checked_frame (one construction site, the refusal keeping its\nexact words and precedence). Heights and bounds in the local frame\nresolve against fully transformed geometry, never a z - origin.z shift.\n\nNo refusal lifted, no post change, no generator change; behavior is\nbyte-identical (the zero-tilt index reproduces the prismatic path\nexactly, move for move).\n\nTests: crates/app/tests/opframe_seam.rs (8) + the seam's inline unit\ntests (6) - identity, zero-tilt exactness, tilted plane run, 90/180\nalignment, alignment x tilt composition, transformed local heights and\nboxes, picks' Phase 1 refusal boundary. Battery green: plane_align (9),\nplane_align_edges (5), axis_align (10), points_align (8), turn_pivot\n(5), area_controls (13), after_op (10), inverted_post (15 - the\ncapability gates), rest_across_setups (7), carried_verify (8). Clippy\nclean on camcraft-app.\n\nRefs #763",
